WEBVTT

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.910
Begin flooding.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:46.870
No abnormalities in water pipes
number one through seven. Valves are OK.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.500
No problems with the resonance lamp.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.760
That's the way, Simon.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:56.970
We've gone under.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.350
Amazing!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.600
We're really underwater!

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.400
You do know I can't swim, right, Mikochi?

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.200
This is an unrehearsed diving test,
but everything seems to be going smoothly for now.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.370
There is much we need to research.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.910
I must obtain detailed data.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:30.380
Well, with my sense of rhythm,
whether we're deep underwater or—

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.460
Konju!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:38.840
The bones' startup period is a delicate time.
Can you please try to focus on your job?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.930
Oh... Okay.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.220
She's a touchy girl, isn't she?

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.680
I'm sure she's just nervous.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.770
Can we keep that rhythm going, please?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.270
Okay, okay.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.700
That's very good.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.080
We'll be coming out of the weeds in a moment.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.960
We got out!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.300
And I'm getting into it!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.350
Wait—It's shaking—

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.430
What does she think she's doing?

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.690
Konju! Stop! You're going too fast!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.980
The woodcutter girl was shocked!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.520
Don't sing!
The woodcutter girl was shocked!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.730
The woodcutter girl was shocked!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.980
Konju!
The woodcutter girl was shocked!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.740
I-I'm sorry. I couldn't help it...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.330
If you're going to keep messing around, give that back.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.750
Simon is easily spooked.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.500
I don't want him to get scared just because you can't control yourself.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.970
You're being obnoxious.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.140
Um...

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.060
This won't do at all.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.940
No matter the stage, a concert won't work without the performers getting along!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.650
Though I will admit that I was in the wrong,

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.490
being spoken to like that only serves to raise tension!

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.990
I mean, look around you. Isn't this beautiful?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.790
Let's take the time to relax and enjoy—

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.920
How vicious!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.300
That's how it works down here.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.340
They don't pay any mind to what we might want.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.550
This is their world.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:57.560
Well, I've made this thing strong enough that it'll take more than that to break it.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:01.860
But if you keep frolicking about,
who knows what might happen.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:08.570
It would be easier to get me to soften my touch
if you were to soften your tongue.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.290
Sorry, that's just how I am.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.500
What are you doing?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.330
Swimming practice.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.560
<i>We've gone pretty deep, but can we still go further?</i>

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.100
She's been this way since the beginning.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:37.400
I feel like I'm drowning in her creepy aura.
We're underwater, so I suppose that's appropriate.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.320
Hey Sen, how about we take a break?

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.240
Simon could probably use a rest, too.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.160
Well, I guess if it's just a short one...

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.000
We've got taro quiche and some apple cookies.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.170
Quiche? That's my favorite!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.010
Sen, do you like quiche?

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.390
I guess.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:17.980
It looks like the new canteen is working well. The tea hasn't leaked at all!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.310
It was made at the Honey House, so...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.150
These cookies... are delicious...

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.950
Sen, Konju makes her living singing around the city, and—

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.790
I know. I saw her singing once when I went to town.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.160
Really? What did you think?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.500
I didn't stick around to hear.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.500
I don't like rowdy places, so...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.840
Well then, you must come and listen sometime.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:53.180
I'll write a sophisticated little ballad, just for you.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.560
Umm...

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.350
Sen.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.310
What is it, Hakumei?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:06.570
Let's go listen to Konju's ballad together.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:13.320
I'm sure she'll make a marvelous song for you. Calm and powerful.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.370
Just like where we are now.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.210
Okay.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.380
That was delicious, Mikochi.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.210
Thanks for the food.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.880
Let's get going soon.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.800
Are you okay?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.090
I can't take this...

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:35.430
Konju, make sure you drum properly, okay?

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.140
I know, I know.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.320
It won't move.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.630
I wonder if Sen will be okay.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.390
And this one as well...

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.520
Mikochi!

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.810
What is it?

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:27.310
It's all my fault that we're stuck down here!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.360
When you come back as a ghost,
make sure to haunt me!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.820
How would I do that?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:37.580
That's right! If we all die together, we'll be spirits together as well!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.080
Here, have some more quiche.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:44.120
<i>She's really eating it.</i>

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.580
It's so good...
<i>She's really eating it.</i>

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.510
<i>The glass and the bones are both in working order.</i>

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.510
<i>The pump system is fine, too.</i>

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.090
<i>The lamp is functioning normally...</i>

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.430
Sen.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.100
H-How was it?

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.740
I have a rough idea of the reason it won't move.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.740
So me getting carried away really is why...

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.160
No. I'm the one who got carried away.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.670
We most likely dove too deep.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.880
Simon got too scared.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:37.340
Even if the lamp works, if he feels upset,
he'll become unable to move.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:45.430
We might not be able to make it home.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:51.070
I've had enough!

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:51.940
Sen!

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:52.730
Yes?

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.490
Can I sing?!

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.400
Wh-What?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.830
I've got an energetic and cheerful song tailor-made for times like this! Okay?!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.700
O-Okay.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.970
Mikochi, do you know the
Woodcutter's Song? Can you do the chorus?

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.170
No problem.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:20.890
One, two...

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:21.430
...three!
One, two...

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.970
The woodcutter—

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.560
It moved just now!

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.980
Maybe Simon likes the rowdy songs better?

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:42.160
The woodcutter girl was shocked!

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.200
Do the next one a bit faster!
I may be a tree, but I'm harder than stone!

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.080
I may be a tree, but I'm harder than stone!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.910
Chip-chip-chop!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:55.050
Not so fast, girl! I won't let you chop me down that easily!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.010
The next line should—
Not so fast, girl! I won't let you chop me down that easily!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.380
Hey, Sen?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.970
Instead of directing us,
why don't you lead the singing?

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.220
Fine.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:12.190
I don't know the lyrics, so I'll just go "la la la."

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.400
We'll all sing la-la-la, then!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.360
Hakumei?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.700
My throat kinda hurts.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.320
What's wrong?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:26.040
For Hakumei, singing is kind of... Well...

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.040
Hakumei!

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:33.670
Will you sing with us?
Even one more person would help.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.420
This is so we can get back to land.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.890
Don't laugh at me.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.240
That was great!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:46.070
That was the Woodcutter's Song, right?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.030
You put a nice spin on it!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.580
Thank you!

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.750
But why'd you change it to la-la-la?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.000
So that anyone could sing along!

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.880
Well, that's it for now.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.300
Have a good night, everyone!

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:01.510
Huh?!

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.970
One more song! One more song!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.230
Actually,

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:18.480
would you mind accompanying me for just one more song?

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.660
This is a quiet song.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.410
It's my first time performing it,
so forgive me if I make a mistake.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.540
Please have a listen to "Rhythm of the Riverbed."

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.890
Did you want long sleeves?

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:00.150
No, I don't really have a preference.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:04.320
I suppose culottes would be best for the bottoms, wouldn't they?

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.610
Sorry, I don't really have an opinion on that either...

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.450
Do you want me to sew in some darts?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.280
Come again?

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.040
How about taking a plunge and showing a little skin?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.120
I'm not sure about that.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:20.630
I sliced up a blueberry. Wanna take a small break?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.130
I'll have some later. I'm going to draw out the design first.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.220
Okie dokes.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:30.510
So why is it that she's suddenly trying to update my wardrobe?

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.970
Um, well...

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:38.980
What did you think?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.650
Your outfit was cute.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.480
That's what you said, remember?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:52.530
So I mentioned that it might be fun if we got you to wear something cute.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.950
So, Sen...

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:55.490
Yes?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.500
If we're using cool-colored fabric,
I think one of these would be good.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.500
This was dyed with indigo only,

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:07.090
and this one used both indigo and a betel dye.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.340
Either one seems...

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.720
Uh, um, well...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:20.350
You're right. Neither of them are a good fit.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.060
Indeed...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.150
That puts us in a bit of a bind, though.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:28.110
I only brought light-colored fabrics with me.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:31.860
Then I suppose I'll go with the purplish one.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:34.660
Can't we dye it again right now?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:39.870
We can, can't we? In that case, we'll make the dye out of...

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.870
Blueberries!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:46.460
But if I only use these, the fabric will end up looking too bright.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:49.510
Shall I go gather some materials?

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:54.390
Can you get me some sawtooth oak acorns or alder cones?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.550
I'm on it!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.180
Sen, will you help me?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.520
Sure.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:03.350
Sen!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:09.150
I'll make some clothes you're sure to love! I hope you're excited!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.200
I can't wait.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.660
I'm sorry.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.830
I made you cater to how I was feeling.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:26.210
I don't remember catering to you at all, though.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.500
R-Really, now?

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.710
This is sawtooth oak.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.350
You can dye things with an acorn cap?

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.140
Yeah.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.100
It'll be finished up with a mordant.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:46.690
If the mordant is potash alum, it'll make it browner, and iron alum is more black-ish.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.020
Wow...

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.030
Interesting. Just like a science experiment.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.910
I can sort of understand why Mikochi is obsessed with it.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.040
I think this should just about do it.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.660
Should we head back?

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.370
Before we do that...

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.920
Ooh. She's really going at it.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:17.180
Mikochi's a real pain when she gets like that.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:23.810
She won't make food,
and she'll ask for so many favors,

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.690
and she won't listen when you tell her to go to bed.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.440
Well, that's just her way of showing her affection.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.780
Just accept it and let her dress you.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:41.330
If we get some more acorns,
will we be able to make a darker dye?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.700
That's right.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.830
Hakumei.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.040
Sorry, but could you help me find a few more?

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.630
I prefer darker colors.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.880
Is that so?

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.090
So...

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.340
You brought all that back?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.470
And there's another pile over there!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:04.350
U-Um, Mikochi...

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.680
Well...

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:10.110
I don't know much about clothes or fashion, but...

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:14.860
I'm really looking forward to seeing what kind of clothes you'll make.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.280
So if there are other things I can help with...

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.040
There are! So, so very many!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:23.700
Huh?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.580
I'll hammer out the last details on this design.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.630
Right.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.800
Make sure to mash up the blueberries and acorns really well.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:35.460
Right.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.260
How's the hot water?

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.170
It's boiled.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:38.380
Let it cool a little.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:39.380
Understood.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:43.010
Hakumei, what about the extra blueberry skins?

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:45.520
They're coming along nicely.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.140
Okay!

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:51.480
Now, shall we finalize the design?

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.400
Oh... let's do that.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.030
This is what I've got now.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:04.160
To keep the design closer to your everyday look,
I kept the culottes and shawl as part of the outfit.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:05.290
Um...

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.660
Could I make one request?

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:10.960
Of course!

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.170
Look...

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:18.720
I'm telling you it's cuter if this part is like this!

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.090
Yes, but... If you were really serious about functionality, then you'd...

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.800
Battle of the perfectionists.
What do you mean by "functionality"?

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.550
What do you mean by "functionality"?

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:29.020
Oi. If we don't start soon, the sun's gonna set.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.900
Leave it in the dye for about thirty minutes.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.900
How do I say this...

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.450
The color is a bit... duller than I expected.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.870
Well, this is only the first stage.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.580
Once we use the mordant,
the colors will change again.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.830
It'll go from a light purple to a blue or navy blue.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:56.840
You dye the fabric again and again until you reach the color you want.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.880
It's a difficult job, huh?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:03.390
I suppose so. And it'll keep changing after the dying is done, too...

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:06.220
But the hard work makes me love the final product even more!

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.890
I see.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.310
So sleepy.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.710
Okay, all done!

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.510
H-How does it look?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.510
Perfect, if I do say so myself.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.720
It's lovely.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.970
Thank you.

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.140
I used glass lanterns as decorations.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:57.150
And I went with a bone motif for the design.
The tie-dying came out pretty well, too.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.980
I can't wait to see how the colors change!

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.610
I'll take good care of it.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.570
Don't take care of it. Wear it!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:14.410
In all honesty, I've never been one for dressing up, but this is surprisingly fun.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.000
Thank you, Hakumei, Mikochi.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:21.340
Why'd you change?

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.010
I didn't have a choice. I don't want the outfit to get dirty.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:28.510
Well, I'd like it if you wore it without worrying too much.

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:29.890
I'll do my best.

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.600
I sure hope it doesn't just gather dust in her dresser.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.190
I wonder if it will.

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.810
What do you think, George?

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.480
Does it look good on me?

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:36.790
If you dive into the tranquil night, you'll hear it

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:44.590
It will gently wash over your body

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:55.720
And you'll see that the rhythm of the riverbed is the rhythm of life

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:11.360
The surface above us softly covers all, just like the starry sky

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:19.160
As our laughter and tears grant our life color,

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:26.800
I pray that we might spend another day of it together
